[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2564834858","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100913#issuecomment-2564834858","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100913","id":2564834858,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Y4EYq","user":{"login":"Mickeon","id":66727710,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2NzI3NzEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/66727710?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon","html_url":"https://github.com/Mickeon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-29T20:46:58Z","updated_at":"2024-12-29T20:46:58Z","body":"I wonder, why would one ever want the existing behaviour enough to warrant it being an optional argument?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2564834858/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2564843176","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100913#issuecomment-2564843176","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100913","id":2564843176,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Y4Gao","user":{"login":"larspet","id":16100387,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MTAwMzg3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16100387?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/larspet","html_url":"https://github.com/larspet","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/larspet/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/larspet/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/larspet/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/larspet/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/larspet/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/larspet/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/larspet/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/larspet/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/larspet/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-29T21:30:05Z","updated_at":"2024-12-29T21:30:05Z","body":"> I wonder, why would one ever want the existing behavior enough to warrant it being an optional argument?\r\n\r\nFor `get_line_column_at_pos()` I can see why it's needed, e.g. in order to put the caret at the last column when clicking past the end of the line. Although I think the argument is backwards, and should be named `p_clamp_position` or something instead.\r\n\r\nThe reason I added the argument to `get_word_at_pos()` was to give them similar API, and not potentially break current uses of it. That said, looking at the other few existing uses of it in the engine, this new functionality would be wanted there too. I can't speak for any user code already utilizing the function however.\r\n\r\nIf wanted, I would not be against not adding this new argument, and instead changing the current behavior of `get_word_at_pos()` instead.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2564843176/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2598654589","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100913#issuecomment-2598654589","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100913","id":2598654589,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6a5FJ9","user":{"login":"kitbdev","id":10054226,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMDU0MjI2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10054226?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev","html_url":"https://github.com/kitbdev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-17T15:49:56Z","updated_at":"2025-01-17T15:49:56Z","body":"The behavior of `get_line_column_at_pos` when allow oob is false shouldn't change. A new parameter can be added to it for horizontal checking, and the existing one's name can be changed.\r\nThis is because there is code that relies on the current behavior of only checking vertical like in `CodeEdit::get_cursor_shape` for the fold icon, and users may be relying on it too. I would also like to use it for gutters, see #101613.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2598654589/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2599270353","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100913#issuecomment-2599270353","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100913","id":2599270353,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6a7bfR","user":{"login":"larspet","id":16100387,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MTAwMzg3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16100387?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/larspet","html_url":"https://github.com/larspet","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/larspet/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/larspet/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/larspet/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/larspet/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/larspet/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/larspet/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/larspet/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/larspet/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/larspet/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-17T21:47:59Z","updated_at":"2025-01-17T21:47:59Z","body":"I removed the optional argument from `get_word_at_pos` since there really wasn't any point to it. The new behavior follows the expected behavior much more anyways.\r\n\r\nInstead, I split the argument in `get_line_column_at_pos` into two (line & column). This way the old behavior is kept (so that e.g. the line-folding `...` icon works), while also optionally allowing to disallow clamping for the column.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2599270353/reactions","total_count":1,"